import LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.FamilyGenericPolynomial

/-!
# Monge's reduction subgroups and the representation theorem for a family

Let `K` be a `p`-adic field, `I = [s_1, …, s_w]_ε^f` a Herbrand invariant, `e = ε p ^ w`, `K_f` the
unramified extension of `K` of degree `f`, `R` its ring of integers with residue field `λ`, `ℛ ⊆ R`
a set of representatives of `λ` containing `0` and `1`, and `π_K` a uniformiser. The semicanonical
polynomials of the family `I / K` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) are the specialisations
`x ^ e + π_K ∑_σ f_σ π_K ^ j x ^ i` of the generic polynomial `f_I` with `d_0 ∈ 𝒟`, `a_σ ∈ ℛ ∖ {0}`,
`b_σ ∈ ℛ` and `c_σ ∈ S_σ`, where `S_σ ⊆ ℛ` represents a quotient `λ / W_σ`
(`IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.semicanonicalPolynomials`, with the `W_σ` as data).
The knowl leaves the subgroups `W_σ` to Monge, *A family of Eisenstein polynomials generating
totally ramified extensions, identification of extensions and construction of class fields*
(arXiv:1109.4617v2, Int. J. Number Theory 10 (2014), doi:10.1142/S1793042114500511, MR 3256847),
and this file defines them as Monge does: Proposition 1 (p. 4), Proposition 2 (p. 5), Lemma 3 and
Definition 1 (p. 6), Algorithm 1 and Remark 1 (p. 7), Proposition 3 (p. 9), Theorem 1 (p. 11) and
Theorem 2 (p. 15) of the arXiv version.

Let `g` be an Eisenstein polynomial of degree `n = e` over `R` and `π` a root of `g`, generating a
totally ramified extension `L` of `K_f` with ring of integers `𝒪_L`. Monge (§2, Proposition 2,
Lemma 3 and Definition 1) changes `π` into `π + θ π ^ (m + 1) + O(π ^ (m + 2))`, `m ≥ 1`. Then
`g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T) = π ^ n Φ(π ^ m T)`, for the ramification polynomial
`Φ(T) = π ^ (-n) g(π T + π)`, has valuation `N = n (φ_{L/K_f}(m) + 1)` (Proposition 1), and the
reduction `S_m` of `π ^ (-N) g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T)` is an additive polynomial over the residue
field (Proposition 2). Writing `N = (j + 1) n + i` with `0 ≤ i < n`, that is `σ = N - n = j e + i`,
the change of uniformiser changes the digit `f_σ` of `π_K ^ (j + 1) x ^ i` by any element of
`(π ^ n / π_K) ^ (j + 1) S_m(λ) = (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(λ)`, and no lower digit; the reduced
polynomials of Definition 1 take this digit in a fixed set of representatives of the cokernel. So
`W_σ` is the image of `θ ↦ (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ)`, for the `m ≥ 1` with `N = σ + n` (there is
at most one, `φ_{L/K_f}` being strictly increasing, and none when the lower ramification break with
`σ = n φ(m)` is not an integer, in which case the digit is not reduced and `W_σ = 0`). It depends on
`g` only through `L` and the class of `π` modulo `π ^ 2` (Monge, Theorem 2), but it is defined here
from `g` and its root `π`, with the valuation `N` computed by the multiplicity of `π`, which is the
valuation of `𝒪_L = R[π]`; it is invariant under isomorphisms of `R[π]`, so it does not depend on
the root of an irreducible `g`. We take the additive subgroup generated by the image, which is the
image itself when `σ + n` is a level, by the first statement of Monge's Proposition 2
(`IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.coe_mongeSubgroup`, in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.MongeAdditive`).

Monge's Theorem 1 has two statements: every totally ramified extension `L / K_f` is generated by a
reduced polynomial, and the number of reduced polynomials generating `L` is
`B_{L/K_f} / #Aut(L / K_f)`. By his Proposition 3 and Remark 1, the reduced polynomials of the
extensions in `I / K`, truncated above the strip `σ ≤ e s_w`, are the semicanonical polynomials.
That the extensions in `I / K` are exactly those generated over `K_f` by the roots of the
semicanonical polynomials, when `K` has residue characteristic `p` and `I / K` is not empty (without
which the converse fails), is stated here
(`IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.MongeRepresentation`) and proved as
`IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeRepresentation`, in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.MongeRepresentationProof`: this is the first
statement of Monge's Theorem 1, with his Proposition 3, his Remark 1 and the converse of his §2.2.
The second statement of his Theorem 1, the number of reduced polynomials generating `L`, is not
proved, and neither is the closing sentence of the knowl, that the ambiguity of the family (LMFDB
`lf.family_ambiguity`) bounds the number of semicanonical polynomials of an extension in `I / K`.
The relation between the Newton polygon of the ramification polynomial of a non-Galois extension and
the Herbrand function (Monge's Proposition 1) is proved in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.RamificationPolygon`. The first step of Monge's
reduction, the normalisation of `d_0`, is proved here, as is the existence of the choices of
representatives, so that the statement is not vacuous.

## Main definitions

* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.aIndices`,
  `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.bIndices`,
  `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.cIndices` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`): the sets
  `𝒜`, `ℬ` and `𝒞` of the generic polynomial.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeShift`: the polynomial `g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T)`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeLevel`: its valuation `n (φ(m) + 1)`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongePolynomial`: Monge's additive polynomial `S_m`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeImage`: the image of
  `θ ↦ (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ)` at the level `σ`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeSubgroup` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`): the
  subgroup `W_σ`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.MongeChoice`: the sets `ℛ` and `𝒟` and a set of
  representatives of `λ / W` in `ℛ` for every additive subgroup `W` of `λ`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.MongeChoice.toSemicanonicalChoice`: the coefficient
  sets they give for given subgroups `W_σ`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials`
  (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`): the semicanonical polynomials with Monge's subgroups `W_σ`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.MongeRepresentation`: the statement of Monge's
  representation theorem for `I / K`.

## Main results

* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.exists_swanSlope_eq_of_mem_cIndices`: the elements
  of `𝒞` correspond to Swan slopes.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.algebraMap_eq_eval_mongePolynomial` and
  `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mem_mongeImage_iff`: the values of `S_m`, and
  Monge's image is the image of `θ ↦ (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ)`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.pow_natDegree_eq_mul_neg_sum`: `π ^ n = π_K v`
  with `v ≡ -d_0`, so the factor of Monge's image is the residue of `(π ^ n / π_K) ^ (j + 1)`.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeSubgroup_algEquiv`: Monge's subgroups are
  invariant under isomorphism.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mongeSubgroup_adjoin_eq_of_minpoly_eq` and
  `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.mem_mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials_adjoin_iff`:
  Monge's subgroups, and so the semicanonical polynomials, do not depend on the choice of a root.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.nonempty_mongeChoice`: Monge's choices exist.
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.exists_mul_pow_ramificationIndex_mem_unitReps` and
  `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.exists_units_mul_pow_ramificationIndex_mem_unitReps`
  (the first step of Monge's reduction, which normalises `d_0`).
* `IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant.isEisensteinAt_of_mem_mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials`
  (the semicanonical polynomials are Eisenstein).
-/

open Algebra Ideal IsLocalRing Polynomial ValuativeRel TauCeti

namespace IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant

variable {p : ℕ} (I : HerbrandInvariant p) {R S S' : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [CommRing S']
  [Algebra R S] [Algebra R S'] (ϖ : R) (𝔪 : Ideal R) (g : R[X]) (π : S) (m σ : ℕ) {a : ℕ → R}
  (e : S ≃ₐ[R] S') (K : Type*) [Field K] [ValuativeRel K] [TopologicalSpace K]
  [IsNonarchimedeanLocalField K] [CharZero K]

/-- The set `𝒜` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) of a Herbrand invariant: the indices `σ = j e + i` of
the `A`-points of the generic polynomial, at the bottom edge `s = m_k` of a geometric band `B_k`
with `k` final in its segment, where the lowest term of index `k` of a polynomial of the family
lies, and which correspond to indices of inseparability (LMFDB `lf.indices_of_inseparability`): for
a `p`-adic field `K` and an extension `E` in the family `I / K`, `σ` is the index of inseparability
`i_{w - k}` of `E / K` (`inseparabilityIndex_eq_of_isInvariantOf`, in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.MongeInseparability`). -/
noncomputable def aIndices : Finset ℕ :=
  {σ ∈ I.genericIndices | I.pointType σ = .A}

/-- The set `ℬ` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) of a Herbrand invariant: the indices `σ = j e + i` of
the `B`-points of the generic polynomial, in a band `B_k` of the index `k` of `i`. -/
noncomputable def bIndices : Finset ℕ :=
  {σ ∈ I.genericIndices | I.pointType σ = .B}

/-- The set `𝒞` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) of a Herbrand invariant: the indices `σ = j e + i` of
the critical `C`-points of the generic polynomial, on the top border `s = σ / e = s_k` of a band,
so that they correspond to Swan slopes. -/
noncomputable def cIndices : Finset ℕ :=
  {σ ∈ I.genericIndices | I.pointType σ = .C}

variable {I σ} in
/-- **The critical `C`-points correspond to Swan slopes**: for `σ ∈ 𝒞`, `σ / e` is one of the Swan
slopes `s_1, …, s_w` of `I`. -/
lemma exists_swanSlope_eq_of_mem_cIndices (hσ : σ ∈ I.cIndices) :
    ∃ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 I.w, I.swanSlope k = σ / I.ramificationIndex := by
  rcases Finset.mem_filter.mp hσ with ⟨hσ, hC⟩
  simpa [hC, point] using (Finset.mem_filter.mp hσ).2

/-- Monge's **shifted polynomial** `g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T)` of a polynomial `g` over `R` at an element
`π` of an `R`-algebra `S`, which is `π ^ n Φ(π ^ m T)` for the ramification polynomial
`Φ(T) = π ^ (-n) g(π T + π)` when `π` is a root of `g` of degree `n`. -/
noncomputable def mongeShift : S[X] :=
  (g.map (algebraMap R S)).comp (C π + C (π ^ (m + 1)) * X)

lemma eval_mongeShift (x : S) : (mongeShift g π m).eval x = aeval (π + π ^ (m + 1) * x) g := by
  simp [mongeShift]

/-- Monge's **level** of `g` at `π` and `m`: the valuation `min_k v_π(c_k)` of the shifted
polynomial `g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T) = ∑_k c_k T ^ k`, for the valuation `v_π` given by the multiplicity
of `π`. For a root `π` of an Eisenstein polynomial `g` of degree `n` generating `L`, it is
`n (φ_{L/K}(m) + 1)` (Monge, Proposition 1). -/
noncomputable def mongeLevel : ℕ∞ :=
  ⨅ k, emultiplicity π ((mongeShift g π m).coeff k)

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Monge's additive polynomial** `S_m` of `g` at `π` and `m ≥ 1` (Monge, §2, Proposition 2): the
reduction modulo `π` of `π ^ (-N) g(π + π ^ (m + 1) T)`, for the level `N` of `g` at `π` and `m`,
that is of `π ^ (-n φ_{L/K}(m)) Φ(π ^ m T)` for the ramification polynomial `Φ`. Its coefficients
are the residues of the quotients of the coefficients of the shifted polynomial by `π ^ N`. -/
noncomputable def mongePolynomial : (S ⧸ span {π})[X] :=
  ∑ k ∈ (mongeShift g π m).support, C (algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π})
    (if h : π ^ (mongeLevel g π m).toNat ∣ (mongeShift g π m).coeff k then
      (exists_eq_mul_right_of_dvd h).choose else 0)) * X ^ k

variable {g π m} in
/-- **The values of Monge's additive polynomial**: if `g(π + π ^ (m + 1) θ) = π ^ N u` for the
level `N` of `g` at `π` and `m`, then `u ≡ S_m(θ)` modulo `π`. -/
lemma algebraMap_eq_eval_mongePolynomial [IsDomain S] (hπ : π ≠ 0) {N : ℕ}
    (hN : mongeLevel g π m = N) {x u : S} (hu : (mongeShift g π m).eval x = π ^ N * u) :
    algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π}) u =
      (mongePolynomial g π m).eval (algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π}) x) := by
  have hNat : (mongeLevel g π m).toNat = N := by
    rw [hN, ENat.toNat_natCast]
  rw [← hNat] at hu
  have hdvd (k : ℕ) : π ^ (mongeLevel g π m).toNat ∣ (mongeShift g π m).coeff k := by
    refine pow_dvd_of_le_emultiplicity ?_
    rw [hNat, ← hN]
    exact iInf_le _ k
  have hu' : u = ∑ k ∈ (mongeShift g π m).support,
      (exists_eq_mul_right_of_dvd (hdvd k)).choose * x ^ k := by
    refine mul_left_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero (mongeLevel g π m).toNat hπ) ?_
    rw [← hu, eval_eq_sum, sum_def, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_
    rw [← mul_assoc, ← (exists_eq_mul_right_of_dvd (hdvd k)).choose_spec]
  rw [hu', map_sum, mongePolynomial, eval_finsetSum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_
  rw [eval_C_mul, eval_X_pow, dite_eq_left (hdvd k), map_mul, map_pow]

/-- **Monge's image** at the index `σ` for a polynomial `g` of degree `n` over `R` with
`g(0) = ϖ d_0`, a uniformiser `ϖ`, an ideal `𝔪` of `R` and a root `π` of `g` in `S`: the classes in
`λ = R / 𝔪` of the `r ∈ R` with `r ≡ (-d_0) ^ (j + 1) u mod π`, where
`g(π + π ^ (m + 1) θ) = π ^ (σ + n) u`, `θ ∈ R`, for an `m ≥ 1` of level `σ + n`, and
`j = σ / n`. Since the level `σ + n` is the valuation of the shifted polynomial, the residue of
`u` is `S_m(θ̄)`, for Monge's additive polynomial `S_m` (`algebraMap_eq_eval_mongePolynomial`), and
this is the image of `θ ↦ (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ)` (`mem_mongeImage_iff`). -/
def mongeImage : Set (R ⧸ 𝔪) :=
  {x | ∃ m, 1 ≤ m ∧ mongeLevel g π m = (σ + g.natDegree : ℕ) ∧ ∃ d r θ : R, ∃ u : S,
    g.coeff 0 = ϖ * d ∧ algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r = x ∧
      (mongeShift g π m).eval (algebraMap R S θ) = π ^ (σ + g.natDegree) * u ∧
        algebraMap R S r - algebraMap R S ((-d) ^ (σ / g.natDegree + 1)) * u ∈ span {π}}

variable {ϖ 𝔪 g π σ} in
/-- **Monge's image is the image of `θ ↦ (-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ)`**: over a domain `S`, the classes
in Monge's image are those of the `r ∈ R` whose residue modulo `π` is
`(-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ̄)` for some `θ ∈ R` and the `m ≥ 1` of level `σ + n`, `S_m` being Monge's
additive polynomial. -/
lemma mem_mongeImage_iff [IsDomain S] (hπ : π ≠ 0) {x : R ⧸ 𝔪} :
    x ∈ mongeImage ϖ 𝔪 g π σ ↔ ∃ k, 1 ≤ k ∧ mongeLevel g π k = (σ + g.natDegree : ℕ) ∧
      ∃ d r θ : R, g.coeff 0 = ϖ * d ∧ algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r = x ∧
        algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π}) (algebraMap R S r) =
          algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π}) (algebraMap R S ((-d) ^ (σ / g.natDegree + 1))) *
            (mongePolynomial g π k).eval (algebraMap S (S ⧸ span {π}) (algebraMap R S θ)) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨k, hk, hl, d, r, θ, u, hd, hr, hu, hr'⟩
    refine ⟨k, hk, hl, d, r, θ, hd, hr, ?_⟩
    rw [← algebraMap_eq_eval_mongePolynomial hπ hl hu, ← map_mul, ← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub,
      Quotient.algebraMap_eq, Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact hr'
  · rintro ⟨k, hk, hl, d, r, θ, hd, hr, h⟩
    have hC : C (π ^ (σ + g.natDegree)) ∣ mongeShift g π k := by
      refine (C_dvd_iff_dvd_coeff _ _).mpr fun i ↦ pow_dvd_of_le_emultiplicity ?_
      rw [← hl]
      exact iInf_le _ i
    have hdvd : π ^ (σ + g.natDegree) ∣ (mongeShift g π k).eval (algebraMap R S θ) := by
      simpa using eval_dvd (x := algebraMap R S θ) hC
    rcases hdvd with ⟨u, hu⟩
    refine ⟨k, hk, hl, d, r, θ, u, hd, hr, hu, ?_⟩
    rw [← Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, ← Quotient.algebraMap_eq, map_sub, sub_eq_zero, h, map_mul,
      algebraMap_eq_eval_mongePolynomial hπ hl hu]

/-- **Monge's subgroup** `W_σ` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) of `λ = R / 𝔪` at the index `σ`, for a
polynomial `g` over `R`, a uniformiser `ϖ` and a root `π` of `g`: the additive subgroup generated
by Monge's image `{(-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1) S_m(θ) | θ ∈ λ}`, which is that image (Monge, Proposition 2).
Changing the uniformiser `π` changes the digit `c_σ` of a semicanonical polynomial by the elements
of `W_σ` and no lower digit, so `c_σ` is taken in a set of representatives of `λ / W_σ`. -/
def mongeSubgroup : AddSubgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (mongeImage ϖ 𝔪 g π σ)

variable {σ} in
lemma mongeSubgroup_eq_bot (h : ∀ k, 1 ≤ k → mongeLevel g π k ≠ (σ + g.natDegree : ℕ)) :
    mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 g π σ = ⊥ := by
  rw [mongeSubgroup, AddSubgroup.closure_eq_bot_iff]
  rintro x ⟨k, hk, hl, -⟩
  exact absurd hl (h k hk)

variable {ϖ g π} in
/-- **The factor of Monge's image is the residue of `(π ^ n / ϖ) ^ (j + 1)`**: for a monic `g` of
degree `n` with coefficients `g_i = ϖ a_i`, `i < n`, and a root `π` of `g`, `π ^ n = ϖ v` with
`v = -∑_{i < n} a_i π ^ i`, which is `-a_0 = -d_0` modulo `π`. So the factor `(-d̄_0) ^ (j + 1)` of
Monge's image is the residue of `(π ^ n / ϖ) ^ (j + 1)`, as in Monge's Lemma 3. -/
lemma pow_natDegree_eq_mul_neg_sum (hg : g.Monic) (ha : ∀ i < g.natDegree, g.coeff i = ϖ * a i)
    (hπ : aeval π g = 0) : π ^ g.natDegree =
      algebraMap R S ϖ * -∑ i ∈ Finset.range g.natDegree, algebraMap R S (a i) * π ^ i := by
  have hsum : ∑ i ∈ Finset.range g.natDegree, g.coeff i • π ^ i =
      algebraMap R S ϖ * ∑ i ∈ Finset.range g.natDegree, algebraMap R S (a i) * π ^ i := by
    rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi ↦ ?_
    rw [ha i (Finset.mem_range.mp hi), smul_def, map_mul, mul_assoc]
  rw [aeval_eq_sum_range, Finset.sum_range_succ, hg.coeff_natDegree, one_smul, hsum] at hπ
  rw [mul_neg, eq_neg_iff_add_eq_zero, add_comm, hπ]

variable {π} in
lemma neg_sum_add_mem_span_singleton {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) :
    -∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, algebraMap R S (a i) * π ^ i + algebraMap R S (a 0) ∈ span {π} := by
  rcases n with _ | k
  · exact absurd hn (lt_irrefl 0)
  rw [Finset.sum_range_succ', pow_zero, mul_one, neg_add, neg_add_cancel_right]
  exact neg_mem <| sum_mem fun i _ ↦
    mem_span_singleton.mpr <| (dvd_pow_self π i.succ_ne_zero).mul_left _

lemma map_mongeShift : (mongeShift g π m).map (e : S →+* S') = mongeShift g (e π) m := by
  have h : (e : S →+* S').comp (algebraMap R S) = algebraMap R S' := RingHom.ext e.commutes
  simp [mongeShift, Polynomial.map_comp, Polynomial.map_map, h]

lemma mongeLevel_algEquiv : mongeLevel g (e π) m = mongeLevel g π m := by
  simp [mongeLevel, ← map_mongeShift, emultiplicity_map_eq]

lemma mongeImage_subset_mongeImage_algEquiv :
    mongeImage ϖ 𝔪 g π σ ⊆ mongeImage ϖ 𝔪 g (e π) σ := by
  rintro x ⟨k, hk, hl, d, r, θ, u, hd, hr, hu, hπ⟩
  refine ⟨k, hk, (mongeLevel_algEquiv g π k e).trans hl, d, r, θ, e u, hd, hr, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [eval_mongeShift, ← e.commutes θ, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, ← map_add, aeval_algHom_apply,
      ← eval_mongeShift, hu, map_mul, map_pow]
  · rw [← e.commutes r, ← e.commutes, ← map_mul, ← map_sub]
    exact mem_span_singleton.mpr <| map_dvd e <| mem_span_singleton.mp hπ

/-- **Monge's subgroups are invariant under isomorphism**: an `R`-algebra isomorphism `S ≃ S'`
mapping `π` to `π'` identifies Monge's subgroups `W_σ` of `g` at `π` and at `π'`. In particular, for
an irreducible `g`, they do not depend on the root `π` of `g` in `K̄`, the rings `R[π]` of the roots
being isomorphic. -/
lemma mongeSubgroup_algEquiv : mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 g (e π) σ = mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 g π σ := by
  refine congrArg AddSubgroup.closure <| subset_antisymm ?_
    (mongeImage_subset_mongeImage_algEquiv ϖ 𝔪 g π σ e)
  simpa using mongeImage_subset_mongeImage_algEquiv ϖ 𝔪 g (e π) σ e.symm

variable [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [IsDomain S] [Module.IsTorsionFree R S] in
/-- **Monge's subgroups do not depend on the root**: for two elements `x` and `x'` of a domain `S`,
integral over an integrally closed domain `R` and with the same minimal polynomial, such as two
roots in `K̄` of an irreducible Eisenstein polynomial over the ring of integers of `K_f`, Monge's
subgroups `W_σ` of `g` at `x` in `R[x]` and at `x'` in `R[x']` agree. -/
lemma mongeSubgroup_adjoin_eq_of_minpoly_eq {x x' : S} (hx : IsIntegral R x)
    (hx' : IsIntegral R x') (h : minpoly R x = minpoly R x') :
    mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 g (⟨x', subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin R {x'}) σ =
      mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 g (⟨x, subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin R {x}) σ := by
  have h' : minpoly R (adjoin.powerBasis' hx).gen = minpoly R (adjoin.powerBasis' hx').gen :=
    (adjoin.powerBasis'_minpoly_gen hx).symm.trans <| h.trans <| adjoin.powerBasis'_minpoly_gen hx'
  rw [← mongeSubgroup_algEquiv ϖ 𝔪 g _ σ
      ((adjoin.powerBasis' hx).equivOfMinpoly (adjoin.powerBasis' hx') h'),
    ← adjoin.powerBasis'_gen hx, PowerBasis.equivOfMinpoly_gen, adjoin.powerBasis'_gen]

/-- **Monge's choices** of coefficients (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) for a Herbrand invariant
`I = [s_1, …, s_w]_ε^f` over a commutative ring `R` with an ideal `𝔪`, the LMFDB's case being the
ring of integers of `K_f` and its maximal ideal, with residue field `λ = R / 𝔪`: a set `ℛ` of
representatives of `λ` containing `0` and `1`, for every additive subgroup `W` of `λ` a set of
representatives of `λ / W` in `ℛ` (Monge's sets `A_m` of representatives of the cokernels of the
maps `θ ↦ η̄ ^ j S_m(θ)`), and a set `𝒟 ⊆ ℛ ∖ {0}` of representatives of `λ^× / (λ^×)^ε`, which
is `{1}` when `gcd(ε, |λ| - 1) = 1` (Monge's set `A_0`, for `(λ^×)^ε = (λ^×)^e`). -/
structure MongeChoice where
  /-- The set `ℛ` of representatives of the residue ring `λ = R / 𝔪`. -/
  reps : Set R
  zero_mem_reps : 0 ∈ reps
  one_mem_reps : 1 ∈ reps
  existsUnique_mem_reps (x : R ⧸ 𝔪) : ∃! r, r ∈ reps ∧ algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r = x
  /-- The set of representatives in `ℛ` of the quotient `λ / W`. -/
  cosetReps : AddSubgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪) → Set R
  cosetReps_subset (W : AddSubgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪)) : cosetReps W ⊆ reps
  existsUnique_mem_cosetReps (W : AddSubgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪)) (x : R ⧸ 𝔪) :
    ∃! r, r ∈ cosetReps W ∧ algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r - x ∈ W
  /-- The set `𝒟 ⊆ ℛ ∖ {0}` of representatives of `λ^× / (λ^×)^ε` from which `d_0` is chosen. -/
  unitReps : Set R
  unitReps_subset : unitReps ⊆ reps \ {0}
  existsUnique_mem_unitReps (u : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ) :
    ∃! d, d ∈ unitReps ∧ ∃ v : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ, algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) d = ↑(u * v ^ I.ε)
  unitReps_eq (h : I.ε.gcd (Nat.card (R ⧸ 𝔪) - 1) = 1) : unitReps = {1}

variable (C : I.MongeChoice 𝔪)

variable {I 𝔪} [𝔪.IsMaximal] in
/-- **Monge's choices exist** for a maximal ideal `𝔪`, such as the maximal ideal of the ring of
integers of `K_f`, so that the statement of Monge's representation theorem is not vacuous. -/
lemma nonempty_mongeChoice : Nonempty (I.MongeChoice 𝔪) := by
  classical
  let s : R ⧸ 𝔪 → R := fun x ↦
    if x = 0 then 0 else if x = 1 then 1 else Function.surjInv Quotient.mk_surjective x
  have hs (x : R ⧸ 𝔪) : algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) (s x) = x := by
    by_cases h₀ : x = 0
    · simp [s, h₀]
    by_cases h₁ : x = 1
    · simp [s, h₁]
    simp only [s, ite_eq_right h₀, ite_eq_right h₁]
    exact Function.surjInv_eq _ x
  have hs₁ : s 1 = 1 := by
    simp [s]
  let H : Subgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ := (powMonoidHom I.ε).range
  let t : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ ⧸ H → (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ := fun c ↦ if c = 1 then 1 else c.out
  have ht (c : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ ⧸ H) : QuotientGroup.mk (s := H) (t c) = c := by
    by_cases h : c = 1
    · simp [t, h]
    · simp only [t, ite_eq_right h]
      exact QuotientGroup.out_eq' c
  refine ⟨{
    reps := Set.range s
    zero_mem_reps := ⟨0, ite_eq_left rfl⟩
    one_mem_reps := ⟨1, hs₁⟩
    existsUnique_mem_reps := fun x ↦ ⟨s x, ⟨⟨x, rfl⟩, hs x⟩, ?_⟩
    cosetReps := fun W ↦ Set.range fun c : (R ⧸ 𝔪) ⧸ W ↦ s c.out
    cosetReps_subset := fun W ↦ Set.range_comp_subset_range _ s
    existsUnique_mem_cosetReps := ?_
    unitReps := Set.range fun c ↦ s (t c)
    unitReps_subset := ?_
    existsUnique_mem_unitReps := ?_
    unitReps_eq := ?_ }⟩
  · rintro - ⟨⟨y, rfl⟩, hy⟩
    rw [hs] at hy
    rw [hy]
  · intro W x
    refine ⟨s (x : (R ⧸ 𝔪) ⧸ W).out, ⟨⟨_, rfl⟩, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · rw [hs, ← QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem, QuotientAddGroup.out_eq']
    · rintro - ⟨⟨c, rfl⟩, hc⟩
      rw [hs, ← QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem, QuotientAddGroup.out_eq'] at hc
      rw [hc]
  · rintro - ⟨c, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨_, rfl⟩, fun h ↦ (t c).ne_zero <| (hs (t c)).symm.trans <|
      (congrArg (algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪)) (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp h)).trans (map_zero _)⟩
  · intro u
    rcases MonoidHom.mem_range.mp (QuotientGroup.eq.mp (ht u).symm) with ⟨v, hv⟩
    refine ⟨s (t u), ⟨⟨_, rfl⟩, v, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · rw [hs, ← powMonoidHom_apply, hv, mul_inv_cancel_left]
    · rintro - ⟨⟨c, rfl⟩, w, hw⟩
      rw [hs, Units.val_inj] at hw
      have hc : c = QuotientGroup.mk u := by
        rw [← ht c, hw, QuotientGroup.mk_mul,
          (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (w ^ I.ε)).mpr (MonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨w, rfl⟩)]
        exact mul_one (QuotientGroup.mk u : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ ⧸ H)
      rw [hc]
  · intro h
    let F : Field (R ⧸ 𝔪) := Quotient.field 𝔪
    have hcop : (Nat.card (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ).Coprime I.ε := by
      rw [Nat.card_units]
      exact Nat.coprime_comm.mp h
    have h₁ (c : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ ⧸ H) : c = 1 := by
      rcases hcop.pow_left_bijective.2 c.out with ⟨y, hy⟩
      rw [← QuotientGroup.out_eq' c, ← hy]
      exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (y ^ I.ε)).mpr (MonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨y, rfl⟩)
    ext d
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
      rw [h₁ c]
      simp [t, hs₁]
    · rintro rfl
      exact ⟨1, by simp [t, hs₁]⟩

variable {I 𝔪} [𝔪.IsMaximal] [Finite (R ⧸ 𝔪)] [ExpChar (R ⧸ 𝔪) p] in
/-- **Monge's reduction step 0** (Algorithm 1), for a residue field `λ = R / 𝔪` finite of
characteristic `p`: for every unit `u` of `λ` there is a unit `θ` of `λ` such that `u θ ^ e`,
`e = ε p ^ w`, is the residue of an element of `𝒟`, since every unit of `λ` is a `p ^ w`-th power
and `𝒟` represents `λ^× / (λ^×)^ε = λ^× / (λ^×)^e`. So for an Eisenstein polynomial `g` of degree
`e` with root `π` and `g(0) = ϖ d_0`, and a lift `θ` of the unit given for `u = d̄_0`, the
polynomial `θ ^ e g(θ⁻¹ X)` (`Polynomial.scaleRoots`) has the root `θ π`, which generates the same
field, and the constant coefficient `ϖ d_0 θ ^ e`, with `d_0 θ ^ e` congruent to an element of
`𝒟`: this normalises the coefficient `d_0` of the `D`-point. -/
lemma exists_mul_pow_ramificationIndex_mem_unitReps (u : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ) :
    ∃ θ : (R ⧸ 𝔪)ˣ, ∃ r ∈ C.unitReps, algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r = ↑(u * θ ^ I.ramificationIndex) := by
  rcases C.existsUnique_mem_unitReps u with ⟨r, ⟨hr, v, hv⟩, -⟩
  rcases (PerfectRing.bijective_frobenius (R := R ⧸ 𝔪) (p := p ^ I.w)).2 (v : R ⧸ 𝔪) with ⟨y, hy⟩
  have hy' : y ^ p ^ I.w = v := hy
  have hyu : IsUnit y :=
    (isUnit_pow_iff (pow_ne_zero I.w (expChar_ne_zero (R ⧸ 𝔪) p))).mp <| hy' ▸ v.isUnit
  have hθ : hyu.unit ^ p ^ I.w = v :=
    Units.ext <| by rw [Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, IsUnit.unit_spec, hy']
  exact ⟨hyu.unit, r, hr, by rw [hv, ramificationIndex, mul_comm I.ε, pow_mul, hθ]⟩

variable {I} [IsLocalRing R] [Finite (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R)] [ExpChar (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R) p] in
/-- **Monge's reduction step 0 for the coefficient `d_0`** (Algorithm 1): over a local ring `R` with
finite residue field of characteristic `p`, for every unit `d_0` of `R` there is a unit `θ` of `R`
with `d_0 θ ^ e` congruent to an element of `𝒟`. For an Eisenstein polynomial `g` of degree `e`
with `g(0) = ϖ d_0` and root `π`, the polynomial `θ ^ e g(θ⁻¹ X)` (`Polynomial.scaleRoots`) has
the root `θ π`, which generates the same field, and the constant coefficient `ϖ d_0 θ ^ e`. -/
lemma exists_units_mul_pow_ramificationIndex_mem_unitReps (D : I.MongeChoice (maximalIdeal R))
    {d : R} (hd : IsUnit d) : ∃ θ : Rˣ, ∃ r ∈ D.unitReps,
      algebraMap R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R) (d * θ ^ I.ramificationIndex) =
        algebraMap R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R) r := by
  rcases exists_mul_pow_ramificationIndex_mem_unitReps D
    (hd.map (algebraMap R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R))).unit with ⟨θ, r, hr, h⟩
  rcases Quotient.mk_surjective (θ : R ⧸ maximalIdeal R) with ⟨t, ht⟩
  have ht' : algebraMap R (R ⧸ maximalIdeal R) t = θ := ht
  have htu : IsUnit t := notMem_maximalIdeal.mp fun h ↦ θ.ne_zero <| by
    rw [← ht', Quotient.algebraMap_eq, Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact h
  refine ⟨htu.unit, r, hr, ?_⟩
  rw [h, IsUnit.unit_spec, map_mul, map_pow, ht', Units.val_mul, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val,
    IsUnit.unit_spec]

variable {I 𝔪} in
/-- The choice of coefficient sets of semicanonical polynomials given by Monge's choices `C` and
subgroups `W σ` of `λ`: the coefficient `c_σ` is taken in the representatives of `λ / W σ`. -/
def MongeChoice.toSemicanonicalChoice (W : ℕ → AddSubgroup (R ⧸ 𝔪)) :
    I.SemicanonicalChoice 𝔪 where
  reps := C.reps
  zero_mem_reps := C.zero_mem_reps
  one_mem_reps := C.one_mem_reps
  existsUnique_mem_reps := C.existsUnique_mem_reps
  subgroup := W
  quotientReps σ := C.cosetReps (W σ)
  quotientReps_subset σ := C.cosetReps_subset (W σ)
  existsUnique_mem_quotientReps σ := C.existsUnique_mem_cosetReps (W σ)
  unitReps := C.unitReps
  unitReps_subset := C.unitReps_subset
  existsUnique_mem_unitReps := C.existsUnique_mem_unitReps
  unitReps_eq := C.unitReps_eq

variable {I 𝔪} in
lemma MongeChoice.cosetReps_bot : C.cosetReps ⊥ = C.reps := by
  refine (C.cosetReps_subset ⊥).antisymm fun r hr ↦ ?_
  rcases C.existsUnique_mem_cosetReps ⊥ (algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r) with ⟨r', ⟨hr', h⟩, -⟩
  rw [AddSubgroup.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at h
  rcases C.existsUnique_mem_reps (algebraMap R (R ⧸ 𝔪) r) with ⟨t, -, ht⟩
  rw [ht r ⟨hr, rfl⟩, ← ht r' ⟨C.cosetReps_subset ⊥ hr', h⟩]
  exact hr'

variable {𝔪} in
/-- The **semicanonical polynomials** (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`) of a Herbrand invariant `I` at
an element `π` of an `R`-algebra `S`, for a uniformiser `ϖ` and Monge's choices `C`: the
polynomials `q` with root `π` that are specialisations `x ^ e + ϖ ∑_σ f_σ ϖ ^ j x ^ i` of the
generic polynomial with `d_0 ∈ 𝒟`, `a_σ ∈ ℛ ∖ {0}`, `b_σ ∈ ℛ`, and `c_σ` in the representatives of
`λ / W_σ` for Monge's subgroup `W_σ` of `q` at `π`. -/
def mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials : Set R[X] :=
  {q | aeval π q = 0 ∧
    q ∈ I.semicanonicalPolynomials ϖ (C.toSemicanonicalChoice (mongeSubgroup ϖ 𝔪 q π))}

variable {I ϖ g π} [NeZero p] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R] in
/-- **The semicanonical polynomials are Eisenstein polynomials**: over a discrete valuation ring
`R` with uniformiser `ϖ`, every semicanonical polynomial of `I` with Monge's subgroups is
Eisenstein at the maximal ideal. -/
lemma isEisensteinAt_of_mem_mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ)
    {D : I.MongeChoice (maximalIdeal R)} (hg : g ∈ I.mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials ϖ π D) :
    g.IsEisensteinAt (maximalIdeal R) :=
  isEisensteinAt_of_mem_semicanonicalPolynomials hϖ hg.2

variable {I 𝔪} [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [IsDomain S] [Module.IsTorsionFree R S] in
/-- **Being semicanonical does not depend on the root**: for two elements `x` and `x'` of a domain
`S`, integral over an integrally closed domain `R` and with the same minimal polynomial, such as two
roots in `K̄` of an irreducible polynomial over the ring of integers of `K_f`, a polynomial is
semicanonical at `x` in `R[x]` if and only if it is semicanonical at `x'` in `R[x']`. -/
lemma mem_mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials_adjoin_iff {x x' : S} (hx : IsIntegral R x)
    (hx' : IsIntegral R x') (h : minpoly R x = minpoly R x') :
    g ∈ I.mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials ϖ (⟨x', subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin R {x'}) C ↔
      g ∈ I.mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials ϖ (⟨x, subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin R {x}) C := by
  have hroot (y : S) (hy : IsIntegral R y) :
      aeval (⟨y, subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin R {y}) g = 0 ↔ minpoly R y ∣ g := by
    rw [← Subalgebra.coe_eq_zero, aeval_subalgebra_coe, minpoly.isIntegrallyClosed_dvd_iff hy]
  simp only [mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, hroot x' hx', hroot x hx, h,
    funext fun σ ↦ mongeSubgroup_adjoin_eq_of_minpoly_eq ϖ 𝔪 g σ hx hx' h]

/-- **Monge's representation theorem** for the family `I / K` (LMFDB `lf.family_polynomial`): if `K`
has residue characteristic `p` (the prime of `I`, as in the knowl) and `I / K` is not empty (as for
the Herbrand invariant of any finite extension of `K`,
`IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.mk_mem_family_visibleHerbrandInvariant`), then for every uniformiser `ϖ`
of the ring of integers `𝒪_{K_f}` of the unramified extension `K_f` of degree `f` of `K` in `K̄` and
all choices `C` of representatives (which exist, `nonempty_mongeChoice`), the extensions in the
family `I / K` are, up to `K`-isomorphism, exactly the fields `K_f(α)` for the roots `α ∈ K̄` of the
semicanonical polynomials over `𝒪_{K_f}`, with Monge's subgroups computed at `α` in `𝒪_{K_f}[α]`. It
is proved as `mongeRepresentation`, in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.LocalField.MongeRepresentationProof`. That every extension in
`I / K` is of this form is the knowl's statement, and the first statement of Monge's Theorem 1
(every totally ramified extension of `K_f` is generated by a reduced polynomial) applied to the
extensions `L / K_f` of the family, with his Proposition 3 and Remark 1, which identify the
truncated reduced polynomials of the extensions in `I / K` with the semicanonical polynomials
(`exists_adjoin_of_isInvariantOf`). Conversely, a root of a semicanonical polynomial generates an
extension with Herbrand invariant `I`, the `A`-terms and the leading term giving the vertices of its
ramification polygon and the other terms lying on or above it (Monge, §2.2;
`isInvariantOf_of_mem_mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials`), as the mass formula of LMFDB
`lf.eisenstein_diagram` presupposes. The converse needs `I / K` not to be empty, which makes `I`
admissible (`isAdmissible_of_isInvariantOf`), since the data of a Herbrand invariant need not be
those of an extension of `K`: for `K = ℚ_2` and `I = (5)_1^1` the family is empty (a ramified
quadratic extension of `ℚ_2` has Swan slope `1` or `2`), while the semicanonical polynomials,
Eisenstein of degree `2`, generate ramified quadratic extensions. `K_f` carries Tau Ceti's
spectral-norm local-field structure. The second statement of Monge's Theorem 1, the number
`B_{L/K_f} / #Aut(L / K_f)` of reduced polynomials generating `L`, is not claimed here and is not
proved, and neither is the closing sentence of the knowl, that the ambiguity of the family (LMFDB
`lf.family_ambiguity`) bounds the number of semicanonical polynomials of an extension in `I / K`. -/
def MongeRepresentation : Prop :=
  letI Kf : IntermediateField K (AlgebraicClosure K) :=
    unramifiedExtension K (AlgebraicClosure K) I.f
  letI : ValuativeRel Kf := finiteIntermediateFieldValuativeRel K (AlgebraicClosure K) Kf
  letI : Algebra 𝒪[Kf] (AlgebraicClosure K) :=
    ((algebraMap Kf (AlgebraicClosure K)).comp (algebraMap 𝒪[Kf] Kf)).toAlgebra
  ringChar 𝓀[K] = p → (I.family K).Nonempty → ∀ ϖ : 𝒪[Kf], Irreducible ϖ →
    ∀ (C : I.MongeChoice (maximalIdeal 𝒪[Kf])) (c : ExtensionClass K), c ∈ I.family K ↔
      ∃ α : AlgebraicClosure K, ∃ E : FiniteExtension K,
        E.1 = (IntermediateField.adjoin Kf {α}).restrictScalars K ∧ Quotient.mk _ E = c ∧
          (I.mongeSemicanonicalPolynomials ϖ (⟨α, subset_adjoin rfl⟩ : adjoin 𝒪[Kf] {α}) C).Nonempty

end IsNonarchimedeanLocalField.HerbrandInvariant
